Licence: MIT; LICENSE and README.md are verbatim upstream root files.

source/ preserves the exact bytes of the original v2.0/source members needed
for COMMAND.COM, EDLIN, DEBUG, FIND, MORE, SORT and FC, including COMLINK and
the historical README.txt. bin/ preserves the seven corresponding v2.0/bin
release files for comparison, not execution. SOURCES.sha256 pins both sets.
No vendored source, line ending, embedded NUL, conditional assembly switch,
message, or copyright notice is changed. Builds execute the source-built
images, not the release binaries. Case-insensitive include aliases exist only
in temporary build directories and contain identical bytes.

There are 57 pinned upstream files: 46 assembly sources/includes, COMLINK,
the release README.txt, seven release binaries, LICENSE and the root README.
COMMAND's own revision is 2.11, so its DOSSYM.ASM/DOSMAC.ASM include names
resolve to the unedited DOSSYM_v211.ASM/DOSMAC_v211.ASM files in the temporary
build directory. The other six programs use the original unsuffixed files.
TCODE2.ASM's Map_call reference requires the v211 international structure.
The original COMSW switches select the TeleVideo/IBM-compatible build and
its 2.11 copyright/banner text; none of that branding is rewritten.

The repository is a historical source snapshot, not an exact release tree.
source/README.txt explains that COMMAND's split-module sources do not
correspond exactly to the release binary. The other sources also carry their
own revision history; see IDENTITY.md for the measured comparison per program.

Build-side loader metadata is explicit: COMMAND uses MZ-to-COM conversion;
SORT uses EXEMOD-style e_maxalloc=1 so its separately allocated sorting
buffer has free memory. Raw COMMAND.MZ and SORT.MZ remain build artifacts.
SORT changes only header bytes 0Ch/0Dh, never instructions, initialized data,
relocations, source, or the preserved release file; see IDENTITY.md and tests.
